    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p38-q26-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Find the value of $c$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$c=2$.",
          "worked": "The horizontal asymptote is $y=c$. The graph has horizontal asymptote $y=2$, so $c=2$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 52
      },
      {
        "id": "p38-q26-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Find the value of $k$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$k=-3$.",
          "worked": "Using the vertical intercept $(0,-1)$ and $c=2$,\n$$\\begin{align*}-1&=k(a^0)+2\\\\-1&=k+2\\\\k&=-3.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 52
      },
      {
        "id": "p38-q26-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "Find the equation of the curve.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$a=2$, so $y=-3\\times2^{-x}+2$.\n\nSubstitute the marked point $(1,\\tfrac12)$ to find the base.",
          "worked": "Using the marked point $(1,\\tfrac12)$,\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac12&=-3a^{-1}+2\\\\\\frac{3}{a}&=\\frac32\\\\a&=2.\\end{align*}$$\nHence $y=-3\\times2^{-x}+2$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 46
      },
      {
        "id": "p38-q26-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "Find the $x$-intercept.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=\\log_2 3-1$, giving the intercept $(\\log_2 3-1,0)$.\n\nSet $y=0$ and solve the exponential equation.",
          "worked": "At the $x$-intercept, $y=0$.\n$$\\begin{align*}0&=-3\\times2^{-x}+2\\\\2^{-x}&=\\frac23\\\\-x&=\\log_2\\!\\left(\\frac23\\right)\\\\x&=\\log_2\\!\\left(\\frac32\\right)\\\\x&=\\log_2 3-1.\\end{align*}$$\nThe intercept is $(\\log_2 3-1,0)$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 62
      }
    ]
  },
